From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:03:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Add the SMC power sensors

The J604 hwmon node lists one temperature (TCMz) and the fan, so the
system power that the other Apple laptops report is missing.

Add the four power keys that macsmc-power's log_power reads, all of which
read on this machine: on 1.606 on AC, PDTR 7.9 W (input), PSTR 7.9 W
(system), PMVR 3.4 W (3.8 V rail) and PHPC 1.5 W. Labels follow
hwmon-common.dtsi and hwmon-laptop.dtsi; node names are in alphabetical
order and no other channel moves.

The other keys those files and the J713 list (temperatures TB0T, TCHP,
TW0P, TH0x, voltages SBAV and VD0R, current ID0R, Ib8f) are left out
until the J604's own key list (debugfs macsmc-hwmon/keys) shows them.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index c6eebebae9..afaf97dcbf 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -173,6 +173,32 @@
 	smc_hwmon: hwmon {
 		compatible = "apple,smc-hwmon";
 
+		/*
+		 * The four power keys macsmc-power's log_power reads, which
+		 * read on this machine (1.606, on AC: PDTR 7.9 W,
+		 * PSTR 7.9 W, PMVR 3.4 W, PHPC 1.5 W). Labels as in
+		 * hwmon-common.dtsi and hwmon-laptop.dtsi.
+		 */
+		power-PDTR {
+			apple,key-id = "PDTR";
+			label = "AC Input Power";
+		};
+
+		power-PHPC {
+			apple,key-id = "PHPC";
+			label = "Heatpipe Power";
+		};
+
+		power-PMVR {
+			apple,key-id = "PMVR";
+			label = "3.8 V Rail Power";
+		};
+
+		power-PSTR {
+			apple,key-id = "PSTR";
+			label = "Total System Power";
+		};
+
 		/*
 		 * On this machine TCMz read the same as the hottest P-core die
 		 * sensor under macOS.
